"""
## Purpose and audience
Purpose: Pin that expect() assertions fire correctly in describe blocks other than the first.
Audience: maintainers of the feature under test.

# expect() across multiple describe blocks Specification

**Feature IDs:** N/A
**Category:** Test harness
**Difficulty:** 2/5
**Status:** Fixed
**Requirements:** N/A
**Plan:** N/A
**Design:** N/A
**Research:** doc/08_tracking/bug/interp_expect_to_equal_swallows_failures_multi_describe_2026-06-15.md

## Overview

`interp_expect_to_equal_swallows_failures_multi_describe_2026-06-15` reported
that in a spec file with two or more `describe` blocks, an `expect(v).to_equal(wrong)`
inside any `it` body **after the first block** was marked PASSED. The failure
was swallowed; `assert_equal` in the same position reported correctly. The
recorded workaround was to ban `expect(...)` from any multi-describe file.

That workaround is the reason this guard exists: a *silently passing* matcher
cannot be caught by an ordinary green spec, so the discrimination evidence for
this file is the deliberate-sabotage run recorded in the bug document — flipping
any one assertion in block 2, 3 or 4 to a wrong value must turn exactly that
example RED. A vacuous harness would keep it green.

Re-checked 2026-09-12: `expect().to_equal()` fires correctly in every block on
both lanes.

## Syntax

```simple
describe "first":  ...
describe "second": expect(v).to_equal(w)   # must be able to FAIL
```

"""

use std.spec


fn zero() -> i64:
    return 0


fn identity(v: i64) -> i64:
    return v


# ============================================================================
# Test Group 1: the first describe block (the always-working control)
# ============================================================================

describe "block 1 — control":
    """
    ## Control

    Single-describe behaviour was never affected; this block establishes the
    baseline the later blocks are compared against.
    """

    it "reports a matching value as equal":
        step("Run an expect() assertion inside a later describe block")
        # @req REQ-SPEC-EXPECT-LATER-BLOCKS-001
        expect(zero()).to_equal(0)


# ============================================================================
# Test Group 2: the block where the defect appeared
# ============================================================================

describe "block 2 — first block after the control":
    """
    ## The defect position

    The original report's exact shape: a value that is 0 compared against a
    different number, in the second describe block.
    """

    it "compares a zero-valued expression in a later block":
        step("Run an expect() assertion inside a later describe block")
        # @req REQ-SPEC-EXPECT-LATER-BLOCKS-002
        val cv1 = zero()
        expect(cv1).to_equal(0)

    it "compares a non-zero expression in a later block":
        step("Run an expect() assertion inside a later describe block")
        # @req REQ-SPEC-EXPECT-LATER-BLOCKS-003
        expect(identity(42)).to_equal(42)

    it "distinguishes two different values in a later block":
        step("Run an expect() assertion inside a later describe block")
        # @req REQ-SPEC-EXPECT-LATER-BLOCKS-004
        expect(identity(42) == 999).to_equal(false)


# ============================================================================
# Test Group 3: a third block, to rule out a two-block special case
# ============================================================================

describe "block 3 — third block":
    """
    ## Depth

    The hypothesis in the record was describe-scoped matcher state that is
    consumed once. A third block pins that no block index is special.
    """

    it "still compares correctly at block three":
        step("Run an expect() assertion inside a later describe block")
        # @req REQ-SPEC-EXPECT-LATER-BLOCKS-005
        expect(identity(7)).to_equal(7)

    it "still distinguishes at block three":
        step("Run an expect() assertion inside a later describe block")
        # @req REQ-SPEC-EXPECT-LATER-BLOCKS-006
        expect(identity(7)).to_not_equal(8)


# ============================================================================
# Test Group 4: text and bool payloads in a later block
# ============================================================================

describe "block 4 — non-integer payloads":
    """
    ## Payload types

    The swallow was reported on integers; these pin text and bool in a late
    block so a type-specific relapse is visible too.
    """

    it "compares text in a later block":
        step("Run an expect() assertion inside a later describe block")
        # @req REQ-SPEC-EXPECT-LATER-BLOCKS-007
        expect("abc").to_equal("abc")

    it "compares bool in a later block":
        step("Run an expect() assertion inside a later describe block")
        # @req REQ-SPEC-EXPECT-LATER-BLOCKS-008
        expect(1 == 1).to_equal(true)
